        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under dinitrogen in a 250 cm3 flask, di-iso-propylamine and toluene were stirred under a carbon dioxide atmosphere until CO2 uptake ceased. CeCl3(DME) was added and the mixture was stirred under CO2 at 40 °C for 1 h. After CO2 absorption ceased, the mixture was filtered at room temperature under dinitrogen; insoluble [NH2iPr2]Cl was discarded. Solvent and excess amine were removed from the filtrate in vacuo (ca. 10−2 Torr). The pale yellow residue was transferred into sealed ampoules under dinitrogen. Colourless crystals were obtained by recrystallization from heptane.",
