      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "A suspension of Ce4(O2CNiPr2)12 (1) in heptane at 22.5 °C was exposed to dry dioxygen for about 15 h. The yellow oxidation product, soluble in heptane even at −30 °C, was recovered by completely removing the volatiles in vacuo and recrystallized from hot heptane. Colourless crystals of 1 also turned yellow on exposure to dioxygen at room temperature in the solid state, but the solid-state oxidized product was amorphous.",
